ion, itchy eyes, and postnasal drip, particularly during the spring and early fall.","He also notes occasional wheezing and shortness of breath triggered by high pollen counts.","Over-the-counter antihistamines and intranasal corticosteroids provide partial relief, but his symptoms continue to affect his work productivity and quality of life."]},{"sid":43629,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Schizophrenia","- Alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency","- Mitochondrial myopathy","- Allergic rhinitis (seasonal)","- Exercise intolerance"]},{"sid":43630,"type":"psh","lines":["- Tonsillectomy (age 12)"]},{"sid":43631,"type":"medications","lines":["Home Medications:","- Risperidone 2 mg PO daily","- Benztropine 1 mg PO BID","- Cetirizine 10 mg PO daily PRN","- Fluticasone propionate nasal spray 2 sprays each nostril daily"]},{"sid":43632,"type":"allergies","lines":["Benztropine (anticholinergic toxicity), Tree pollen, Grass pollen"]},{"sid":43633,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Mother with mitochondrial myopathy","- Father with alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency and early-onset emphysema","- Maternal uncle with schizophrenia","- Paternal grandmother with liver cirrhosis of unknown etiology"]},{"sid":43634,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never smoker.","Alcohol: Social (1-2 drinks per week).","Occupation: Freelance graphic designer (previously construction laborer)."]},{"sid":43635,"type":"other_studies","lines":["Skin testing confirms sensitivity to multiple aeroallergens, including grass, tree, and weed pollens."]},{"sid":43636,"type":"plan","lines":["After discussing treatment options, the patient elects to begin a long-term course of allergen immunotherapy involving regular subcutaneous injections of gradually increasing doses of the relevant allergens."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":10794,"date":"2021-01-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Neurology","attending":"Dr. Michael Okafor","cc":"Progressive difficulty keeping up with coworkers during physical labor over th