hin, with bilateral ptosis and mild weakness of the proximal limb muscles.","Extraocular movements are restricted in multiple directions.","Cardiopulmonary examination is normal."]},{"sid":43646,"type":"labs","lines":["Laboratory studies reveal elevated creatine kinase, lactate levels persistently high at rest and after minimal exertion, and normal thyroid function."]},{"sid":43647,"type":"pathology","lines":["A muscle biopsy with modified Gomori trichrome stain reveals irregularly shaped muscle fibers with subsarcolemmal collections of abnormal mitochondria."]},{"sid":43648,"type":"other_studies","lines":["Electromyography shows a myopathic pattern."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":10793,"date":"2023-01-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Pulmonology","attending":"Dr. Priya Patel","cc":"Progressive shortness of breath over the past 18 months with dyspnea on minimal exertion despite never smoking.","order":2,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[5051],"sections":[{"sid":43649,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Progressive shortness of breath over the past 18 months with dyspnea on minimal exertion despite never smoking."]},{"sid":43650,"type":"hpi","lines":["The patient returns with progressive dyspnea in the context of known Alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency and prior evaluation for mitochondrial myopathy.","He reports previously jogging regularly but now becomes winded even after walking two blocks.","He endorses occasional mild chest tightness but denies chest pain, wheezing, hemoptysis, or cough."]},{"sid":43651,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Allergic rhinitis (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Mitochondrial myopathy (diagnosed 2021-01-15)","- Schizophrenia","- Alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency","- Allergic rhinitis (seasonal)","- Exercise intolerance"]},{"sid":43652,"type":"psh","lines":["- Tonsillectomy (age 12)"]},{"sid":43653,"type":"medications","lines":["Home Medications:","- Risperidone 2 mg PO daily","- Benztropine 1 mg PO BID","- Cetirizine 10 mg PO daily PRN","- Flut